  "estimand": "The causal effect or correlation strength of opponent next-possession PPP and own-sequence PPP (at various lags) on the probability or magnitude of a play type being assigned an 'AVOID' label.",
  "unit": "Play type instances (defined by initiator and play type) across all NBA teams and seasons.",
  "sample": "All play-type possession records from NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 regular seasons and playoffs, and complete portions of 2025-26 regular season and playoffs. Data will be aggregated to the play-type level (e.g., 'LeBron James Post-Up').",
  "power": "The study aims for 80% power to detect a medium effect size (e.g., R-squared of 0.10 in a regression model) for the influence of next-possession PPP on AVOID labels, assuming sufficient variability in both the independent and dependent variables. Sample size will be driven by the total number of distinct play-type instances observed.",
  "controls": "Control for relevant game context variables such as quarter, score differential, time remaining, home/away status, opponent strength, and the identity of the team executing the play. If possible, control for the 'expected' PPP of the play type itself to isolate the effect of *subsequent* possessions.",
  "falsification": "A falsification test could involve examining if random permutations of next-possession PPP values or own-sequence PPP values show a similar relationship with AVOID labels. Additionally, if the AVOID label generation mechanism is known, checking if the identified factors are explicitly part of that mechanism would serve as a falsification test if the hypothesis is that these factors *implicitly* drive the labels.",
  "multiplicity": "Given that multiple lags will be tested (e.g., next possession, two possessions later) and potentially multiple play types, a Bonferroni correction or False Discovery Rate (FDR) adjustment will be applied to p-values to account for multiple comparisons.",
  "decision_rule": "The hypothesis will be considered 'supported' if statistically significant (p < 0.05 after multiplicity adjustment) and substantively meaningful effects (e.g., standardized regression coefficients > 0.1) are observed for opponent next-possession PPP or own-sequence lags in predicting AVOID labels, consistent with the hypothesized direction.",
  "data_version": "NBA 2022-23, 2023-24, 2024-25 (complete), NBA 2025-26 (partial, up to 2026-06-19 for playoffs and 2026-04-13 for regular season)."
 }
}

